# The two committed solver profiles are RMG output, written by Python's csv writer, which
# terminates every line CRLF on every platform. `git diff --check` therefore flags all 1587
# lines of them as whitespace errors -- a false positive that buries any real one.
#
# `whitespace=cr-at-eol` says the CR is intended here, which is the true statement. The
# alternative fixes are both worse: stripping the CRs edits a byte-preserved measurement
# artifact to satisfy a linter, and marking the files binary would silence the check by
# making the numbers undiffable to a reviewer, which is the opposite of why they are tracked.
#
# Deliberately scoped to these two paths. Whitespace complaints elsewhere in the repo are
# other tickets' and are not silenced from here.

prof-with/solver/simulation_1_3.csv     whitespace=cr-at-eol
prof-without/solver/simulation_1_3.csv  whitespace=cr-at-eol
